@title bit Generations - Boundish (Japan)
@file Bit Generations Boundish (J).gba
@game BVDJ
@chip SRAM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: nothing is written to SRAM through the menus, the court select and a whole VS CPU match on POOL FLOWER won 5-2 and quit with B (checked in dingbat-bios with a screen-tracking paddle over ~9,900 frames: the court select is unchanged after it and the SRAM still blank); the first save must come later (more courts or modes), not found in budget

# Health warning (A) > logo > PRESS START > VS CPU > COURT SELECT (only POOL
# FLOWER on a blank cart) > READY TO GO? A > the serve (A), UP held 30 frames
# to return the CPU's first shot (return), the scoreboard, the CPU's serve.
# Finding (cpu_serve, f2968): mgba is a frame ahead (SLIP -1, its ball 4 px
# further on) of dingbat-bios and the second reference, which agree. The match's frame counter
# (0x03001B9C, +1 per main-loop pass) is already one ahead in mgba at the
# READY screen and two ahead after the first point: dingbat-bios and the
# second reference both drop a frame more than mgba on the match load and
# again on the point-scored transition (stalls of 4 frames against mgba's 3
# at f2727), the §29 kind of mGBA under-charge. From the CPU's serve on, the
# same inputs play a different rally in mgba (the bot's winning match
# replays frame for frame in dingbat-bios and the second reference, but mgba
# loses it).

[new]
wait 300
press A
wait 500
wait 300
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint press_start window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint mode_menu window=30
press A
wait 120
checkpoint court_select window=30
press START
wait 180
checkpoint ready window=30
press A
wait 120
wait 120
press A
wait 60
wait 120
press UP hold=30
wait 36
checkpoint return window=10
wait 150
checkpoint scoreboard window=10
wait 300
checkpoint cpu_serve window=10
